    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Bright and spacious five-bedroom semi-detached residence in the highly regarded Glen Ri development, Ballina.\n\nBeautifully presented throughout, No. 48 offers generous and versatile accommodation over two floors, making it an excellent option for a growing family, first-time buyer or anyone seeking additional space for home working or guests. \n\nGlen Ri is a well-established residential development conveniently located within walking distance of Ballina town centre and its excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants, schools and everyday amenities.\n\nThe River Moy, internationally renowned for its salmon fishing, is close by, while Ballina Golf Club is virtually on the doorstep, giving No. 48 an excellent combination of town convenience, recreation and family living.\n\nGround Floor: Entrance hallway, spacious living room with open fireplace, kitchen/dining area with access to the rear garden, utility room, guest WC and a versatile fifth bedroom/home office.\n\nFirst Floor: Four bedrooms, including a generous master bedroom with ensuite, together with the main family bathroom.\n\nFeatures: \n\n•Spacious 5-bedroom semi-detached home\n•Highly regarded Glen Ri development\n•Generous master bedroom with ensuite\n•Four bedrooms upstairs plus ground-floor bedroom/home office\n•Family bathroom plus guest WC\n•Bright kitchen/dining area with direct garden access\n•Separate utility room\n•Spacious living room with open fireplace\n•Large private enclosed rear garden not overlooked\n•Patio area ideal for outdoor dining and entertaining\n•Ample off-street parking\n•PVC double-glazed windows\n•Oil-fired central heating & open fire\n•BER C/130 sqm approx.\n•Fiber broadband\n•Mains water/sewage\n•Ballina Golf Club close by\n•Convenient to the River Moy\n•Walking distance of Ballina town centre and amenities\n•Built by respected local builders Judge Brothers\n"
      },
